   "title": "Shipping in the Japanese Empire During October 1938",
   "doc_type": "consular shipping report",
   "start_page": 1,
   "end_page": 27,
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1938-11-18",
   "from": "William C. Affeld Jr., American Vice Consul, Kobe",
   "to": "U.S. Department of State",
   "about": "Reports developments in Japanese shipping during October 1938.",
   "summary": "The report covers new ship orders, shortages of materials and labor, port expansion in Manchuria and Japan, proposed consolidation of shipping companies, and new passenger and freight services. It reviews Kokusai Kisen's finances, weather disruptions, charters, freight and bunker coal rates, shipbuilding loans, whaling and fishing incidents. Tables list vessels under construction and the distribution of merchant tonnage, followed by sources.",
